{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108628","id":2666681697,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6e8lVh","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108628","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108628.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108628.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108628","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108628/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108628/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108628/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/c4f472ee9acd8f3ef2f824920a91de8d00365705","number":108628,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix incorrect projection matrix for GI","user":{"login":"retrotails","id":10767978,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzY3OTc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10767978?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails","html_url":"https://github.com/retrotails","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"so I think this problem was a *lot* simpler than I thought. it looks like when these lines were written originally, the column order was backwards. `[0][2]` and `[1][2]` are both always 0.0 in my testing, unused elements of the matrix as far as I can tell, while `[2][0]` and `[2][1]` appear to be the intended ones.\r\n\r\nnote that this fixes voxel GI and SDFGI, but *not* screen space effects. thus, this is only a partial fix for https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108508. these exact same lines also exist in `ss_effects.cpp`, and applying the same fix here *does* fix the X axis, but it does not fix the Y axis, so I'm leaving it as-is for someone else to tackle, because I think at least SSR might need more work than just this projection fixed in order to support an offset frustum.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-07-15T09:13:08Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T11:53:51Z","closed_at":"2026-03-23T11:53:44Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e8a87b29d6b0bda92b92b5e057942c6b9efb032a","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"retrot